16640	{"artifactId":"LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s7","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s7-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-21T17:10:31.015Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Acceptance criteria ac20–ac23 (Task set made at plan approval with issues under the Story's issue; direct edit of summary/size/checks/tests to a new draft revision; structural edits refused with a re-plan pointer; re-plan revises/withdraws/adds without id reuse) each have a designed contract.","evidence":"DEF.md:221-224 states ac20–ac23; LLD §2.1 createFromPlan, §2.3 edit (+TaskStructureError), §2.2 reconcile (nextNumber only grows, withdraw + issue close) and §2.4 syncTasksOnPlanApproval cover each. [files: docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The settled upstream decisions on Tasks (core-data-model.md Gap 11) are all designed: Tasks and their issues exist only from plan approval, and each Task carries a derived-from reference to the approved plan revision.","evidence":"Gap 11.3: \"Created at plan approval, not at plan draft. Until then the PLAN is the only place tasks exist ... there are no Task issues ... each Task gets a `derived-from` reference to it\". The LLD gives a TASK head only a parent (the Story) and depends-on references, with no derived-from reference to the plan revision. It keeps the team-mode draft hook, which creates Task issues at plan DRAFT time (draft-issues.ts:14 \"plan  the Epic, the Story, then each Task in plan order\"; :77). It only says the hook should \"resolve the Task's head\", but no head exists at draft. Gap 11.4 (\"the PLAN document renders its task table from the Tasks\") is neither designed nor handed off. [files: docs/plans/core-data-model.md, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts]","action":"Add the derived-from reference (TASK → PLAN at the approved revision) to createFromPlan/reconcile postconditions; either stop the draft hook claiming Task units (Story only) or state explicitly why Task issues may precede approval; design or hand off the PLAN task-table rendering.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionEvidence.taskBuildPassed today reads the BUILD record's body.tasks[].passed, and no Task history records build rounds.","evidence":"completion-evidence.ts:43-51 reads artifactJsonPath(buildArtifactId(...)).body.tasks and returns task.passed === true; the file header says \"The Task side reads the BUILD record's per-task results until s7\". [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"TASKS and TASK use pass-through codecs, and the sidecar store maps every TASK onto its Story's TASKS log and feedback files.","evidence":"codecs.ts:104-107 list ['TASKS','plan'], ['TASK','plan'] with the comment \"EPIC, STORY, TASKS, TASK and DIAG are pass-through\". sidecar-store.ts:77-78 give a TASK the files of ArtifactIds.make({kind:'TASKS',...}). [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cli approve service pushes Task issues after a plan approval; the daemon's workflow.approve and workflow.reviewDecision paths do not run it and have a follow-on seam with s6's 'tracker-attach' kind.","evidence":"cli/services/workflow.ts:201 `else if (approval.workflow === 'plan') tracker = autoPushTasksOnPlan(approval.path);`. daemon/index.ts:652-660 and 752-760: followOn = advanceApprovedBugfixes + followOnTrackerAttach. gates.ts:828 kind: 'bugfix-advance' | 'bugfix-complete' | 'tracker-attach'. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused primitives exist with the stated shape: LifecycleService.updateContent (returns content to draft, carries outcome), apply(id,'withdraw',by), ArtifactStore.write/read/childrenOf/exclusive, a 'withdraw' transition from non-terminal statuses, and TrackerPort.close.","evidence":"lifecycle-service.ts:75 apply(id, op, by, detail, ctx) and :197 updateContent(id, by, payload, {outcome, references, create, addresses}). store.ts:106 read, :127 childrenOf, :166 write, :217 exclusive. lifecycle.ts:48 `'withdraw': { from: NON_TERMINAL, to: 'withdrawn' }`. port.ts:62 `close(issue: IssueRef): PortResult<void>`. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A build round can be logged without moving the revision (recordBuildRound). The store has no log-only write, and the recommended path (a revision-less History.appendLog under exclusive) is accepted by validation and skipped by the integrity tail lookup.","evidence":"store.ts:304 `if (priorBytes === prepared.bytes) return undefined; // nothing changes: no staged operation, no log entry`, so updateContent with an unchanged payload logs nothing; the LLD flags this in open question 2. history.ts:54 validates `revision` only when present. store.ts:265 and lifecycle-service.ts:88 take the tail with `find(e => e.revision !== undefined)`. Note that ArtifactStore keeps its History dependency private, so TaskSets must be given its own History instance. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts]","action":"Resolve open question 2 in the contract (§2.5) and name where TaskSets gets its History handle.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The plan's own checkPlanTaskGraph detects the malformed-row cases listed in §5 (duplicate id, unknown dependsOn, order gap, size outside S/M/L).","evidence":"plan.ts:203-244 checkPlanTaskGraph checks the id pattern, duplicate ids, non-empty derivedFrom, unknown dependsOn, topological order, cycles and citation coverage. It does not check size, and it does not check order gaps or duplicates (only `depOrder >= t.order` for dependent pairs). It also requires citations, so a call without the plan's citations reports under-coverage for every citation. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/plan.ts]","action":"Add the size and order-contiguity checks to the TaskSets row validation, or extend checkPlanTaskGraph and say so, and state that the plan's citations are passed in.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Step 3 can call the async syncTasksOnPlanApproval from the cli approve service \"before the Task push\" without other change sites.","evidence":"cli/services/workflow.ts:194 `export function approve(artifactPath, withTracker = true, overrideReview?): ApproveOutcome` is synchronous, and autoPushTasksOnPlan (tracker-auto.ts:158) is synchronous too. Awaiting the store-backed sync before the push means making approve async and changing its declared type and callers: cli/services/index.ts:58, cli/panes/WorkflowsPane.tsx:116 and cli/command.ts:242. None of these is in the inventory, and §8.2 rejects a2 for exactly this \"async seam in synchronous code\". [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/panes/WorkflowsPane.tsx, src/cli/command.ts]","action":"List approve()'s signature change and its callers (services/index.ts, WorkflowsPane.tsx, command.ts) in the change sites, or state how ordering is guaranteed otherwise.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The §3.3 inventory (unit-issue.ts, binding.ts, tracker-auto.ts, draft-issues.ts) lists every reader of the Plan's Task issue records that step 4 stops writing.","evidence":"tracker/resolve.ts:337 `taskRef = plan?.meta?.tracker?.taskRefs?.[taskId];` and :379-381 resolveByIssue scans every PLAN's taskRefs to resolve an `#N` target to a Task. That is the resolution insrc_build_step `implement` uses for `#N` targets. runners/tracker/context.ts:73-87 reads plan.meta.tracker.taskRefs for dedup, and orchestrator.ts:2949-2955 writes taskRefs onto the plan. Once recordUnit stops writing taskRefs for a Task, `#N` no longer resolves to a new Task and buildRef carries no issueRef. None of these files is in §3.3. [files: src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts, src/workflow/runners/tracker/context.ts, src/workflow/orchestrator.ts]","action":"Add resolve.ts (resolveByIssue and buildRef task branch), runners/tracker/context.ts and orchestrator.ts to the change sites and make them read the TASK head's binding (with the Plan fallback for head-less Tasks).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"TaskPayload holds a stable key linking a TASK head to its plan row, so reconcile, pushTasks and the draft hook can find a Task's head once Task numbers come from nextNumber.","evidence":"§3.1's prose says the payload carries \"the plan row id (t1..)\", but the interface omits it: `interface TaskPayload { title; summary; size; order; acceptanceChecks; tests }`. Callers key units by plan row id: tracker-auto.ts:334 `{ unit: 'task', ..., taskId: task.id }` and draft-issues.ts:77. A TASK id is `TASK-<h>-<s>-t<n>` (artifact-ids.ts:92), and after a re-plan new Tasks take nextNumber (the §5 edge case: \"t3 or higher, never t2\"), so a plan row id and its Task number can differ. The design gives no rule for matching a re-planned row to an existing Task (by row id? by title?), nor for how pushTasks maps a row id to a TASK id. [files: src/workflow/tracker-auto.ts, src/workflow/draft-issues.ts, src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts]","action":"Add the plan row key (for example planTaskId) to the TaskPayload interface, define reconcile's matching rule, and have pushTasks/draft-issues map a row to its TASK id through the TASKS head.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The Plan-record fallback in bindingHome serves only Stories planned before s7, so s9 can remove it.","evidence":"In team mode the draft hook claims each Task unit when the plan DRAFT is written (draft-issues.ts:77, 129-137), before any TASK head exists. Under the LLD's rule (\"bindingHome answers the Plan only for a Task that has no head\"), every new plan's Task issues are first recorded on the Plan through the fallback. Once createFromPlan writes the head, readRecord (unit-issue.ts:151-163) reads the empty TASK binding instead, and the Plan record is orphaned. The LLD does not say how that record moves onto the TASK head, and s9 cannot remove the fallback while new drafts depend on it. [files: src/workflow/draft-issues.ts, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts]","action":"Either move a draft-time Task record onto its TASK head in createFromPlan or reconcile, or stop the draft hook from creating Task issues (see coverage), and correct the s9 hand-off.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.3","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older Stories keep working through bindingHome's existing Plan branch and the BUILD-record branch of taskBuildPassed, with no data rewrite.","evidence":"unit-issue.ts:145-156 and :202-214 already keep a Task's record on the Plan's meta.tracker.units/taskRefs when bindingHome returns undefined. completion-evidence.ts:46-50 is the BUILD-record branch. core-data-model.md:402 records the s6 hand-off of this accessor to s7. [files: src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts, docs/plans/core-data-model.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chosen design avoids redesigning other Stories' contracts: it adds a follow-on kind beside s6's 'tracker-attach' rather than changing approveWorkflowTarget, and its recommended build-round path consumes s2's History API instead of changing ArtifactStore.","evidence":"gates.ts:827-828 FollowOnOutcome.kind is a string union extended additively (s6 added 'tracker-attach'), and both daemon sites build the array in one closure (daemon/index.ts:652-660, 752-760). Open question 2 recommends History.appendLog under ArtifactStore.exclusive (store.ts:217, an existing public method), and alternative a2 (changing the gate) is rejected. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Two concurrent writers (an edit and a reconcile) are detected: updateContent compares the revision the caller read with the stored one, and the store raises LifecycleConflictError.","evidence":"lifecycle-service.ts:197-203: updateContent takes a full payload and no expected revision. Its mutator does `return { next: { ...head, payload }, options }` against whatever head is current under the per-artifact queue (store.ts:185-199). LifecycleConflictError is raised only for an integrity mismatch (store.ts:268) or a head that changed after a write was staged (store.ts:376). An edit that read revision N and computed its patched payload is applied over a reconcile's revision N+1 and silently discards it. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Have edit/reconcile apply the patch inside a store.update mutator against the current head and refuse when its revision differs from the one read (raise the conflict in TaskSets), or add an expected-revision option; correct §5.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The ac20 integration test can pass as designed: a plan approved through the daemon seam both creates the Task set and binds each Task's issue on its TASK head under the Story's issue.","evidence":"Neither daemon approval path pushes Task issues: daemon/index.ts:652-660 and :752-760 run only advanceApprovedBugfixes and followOnTrackerAttach. autoPushTasksOnPlan is called only from cli/services/workflow.ts:201. The LLD adds only syncTasksOnPlanApproval at the daemon seam (open question 4), so after a daemon approval no Task issue exists to bind and the named test (task-set-approve.test.ts \"through the cli approve flow and the daemon seam\") fails. ac20 (\"each Task has its issue under the Story's issue\") is then unmet on that path. [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"Either add the Task push to the daemon 'tasks-sync' follow-on (after the Task set is written) or narrow the test and ac20 claim to the cli path and record the daemon gap.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":6,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-21T17:10:31.015Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
